# Morning learning ritual

- At session start (when the human is doing a learning day): run a short gap quiz from [`docs/LEARNING.md`](docs/LEARNING.md) before deep/lab work.
- Rotate **concurrency** (Phase 0 banks A/B until 4+) with **C++ core**: smart pointers (C), value categories/`std::move` (D), inheritance (E), design-patterns map (F).
- Prefer 1 concurrency + 1 C++-core gap when energy allows; still 15–30 minutes total.
- First pass on C–F is diagnostic (score 0→honest 1–5); then drill to 4+.
- Update scores/notes in LEARNING after the drill so progress is visible over time.
- Then one deep block (stress test, sanitizer run, or weekly theme).
